# Ship EAS Update to production + preview

The installed **preview** build reads the `preview` channel; App Store / Play builds read `production`. Ship both so TestFlight/internal preview and store users both get the update:

```bash
eas update --channel production --environment production --message "<short why>"
eas update --channel preview --environment preview --message "<short why>"
```

Force-close / reopen picks up the OTA for that build’s channel.

## Server / web

- **Dripn-Server**: push `main` → Render auto-deploy
- **Vercel** when a web project is involved

## When to skip OTA

- Docs-only / non-app changes with no runtime effect
- Native-only work that needs `eas build` instead (still say so; OTA cannot replace the binary)

## Prefer Update over full builds

- Prefer `eas update` for JS/TS, styles, locales, and bundled assets
- Recommend `eas build` only for new native modules/plugins, native `app.json` / `eas.json` fields, icons, splash, or permissions

## Reply format after shipping

1. Confirm **production** and **preview** update group URLs (or IDs)
2. Note Render (and Vercel if relevant) for backend/web
3. Remind: force-close / reopen the app to pick up the update
